{
  "Version": 1,
  "Title": "NurbsCONTACT AES — manuscript argument",
  "Nodes": [
    {
      "Id": "question",
      "Caption": "Engineering question",
      "Title": "Narrow clearances make the required contact accuracy depend on the response being resolved. An implicit solver can use its nonlinear acceptance tests to decide when a contact-force estimate needs refinement.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/Residual-Aware-CAD-Contact.tex — Introduction, first two paragraphs"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Align the abstract and introduction on the order of the main contributions. The abstract currently leads with continuous detection, while the numbered contributions start with residual-controlled HHT and reuse."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 60
    },
    {
      "Id": "hht",
      "Caption": "Residual-controlled HHT",
      "Title": "Force enclosures bound the HHT residual at each trial. The solver tightens the force estimate when its uncertainty prevents a convergence or line-search decision.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/method.tex — sec:method, eq:residual, eq:resid-error, alg:trial"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Distinguish convergence from descent. Acceptance uses the residual upper bound against the tolerance lower bound. Descent uses the trial upper bound against the current lower bound."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 180
    },
    {
      "Id": "reuse",
      "Caption": "Revalidated contact reuse",
      "Title": "Relative point-travel bounds revalidate stored pair exclusions. Previously evaluated gear points can propose ray intersections, with the root and ray bounds checked again at the current trial.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/method.tex — sec:gear-root, eq:probe-error, eq:transport\ndocs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — sec:ablation"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Describe this contribution as reuse under a force budget. Report the cam benefit together with the gear cases in which extra refinements offset it."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 300
    },
    {
      "Id": "matched",
      "Caption": "Matched-accuracy cost",
      "Title": "The mechanism-specific tests compare query cost at joint RMS position and force targets. Tuned section baselines achieve similar errors and online times to native CAD on the tested gears.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — sec:industrial, tab:industrial, fig:cam, fig:spur, fig:reducer"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Keep setup and online time distinct. Name the general triangle BVH and the structure-aware polyline separately when discussing cost."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 420
    },
    {
      "Id": "onset",
      "Caption": "Prescribed-motion onset",
      "Title": "The general STEP query bounds contact onset for prescribed rigid motion. It reports a verified inactive interval and an upper time bound when a feasible point pair is verified against the activation distance.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/method.tex — Contact onset on a prescribed motion, fig:event-schematic\ndocs/AES/generic-contact-results.tex — sec:general-contact, tab:cam-onset\ndocs/AES/generic-assembly-results.tex — tab:production-contact"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Report complete, wider-than-target and unresolved outcomes distinctly. The loaded spur and reducer segments already start inside the activation layer."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 540
    },
    {
      "Id": "gpu",
      "Caption": "Independent GPU study",
      "Title": "The sampled-contact GPU experiments assess how surface representation, contact-region grouping, and stiffness assignment affect mechanism response. In the coupled reducer, the pair-stiffness model improves agreement in shaft-level outputs with refined RecurDyn.",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/sampled-dynamics-results.tex — sec:sampled-dynamics, tab:refined-reducer"
        },
        {
          "Title": "Revision note",
          "Body": "Identify this as a separate sampled-contact solver when discussing timings or response agreement. State the stiffness assignment and common output interval beside the reported RMS differences."
        }
      ],
      "X": 415,
      "Y": 660
    },
    {
      "Id": "oscillator",
      "Caption": "Published oscillator",
      "Title": "The exact scalar force callback reproduces all 100 contact transitions over 50 periods",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/published-validation.tex — sec:oscillator, tab:oscillator, fig:oscillator\nThis benchmark checks integration through repeated contact and release. The method section supplies the enclosure argument."
        }
      ],
      "X": 75,
      "Y": 180
    },
    {
      "Id": "ablation",
      "Caption": "Force and reuse ablation",
      "Title": "The 20 s cam run records 692 revalidated exclusions and 119 precision refinements at a 500 µs step",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — sec:ablation, cam paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "X": 75,
      "Y": 300
    },
    {
      "Id": "matched-table",
      "Caption": "Matched gear results",
      "Title": "At 5 µs, the spur CAD and 1024-segment polyline give 0.037 µm RMS transmission error and 0.89% relative RMS force error, with median online times of 4.03 s and 3.94 s",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — tab:industrial, Single-stage spur pair\nFor the reducer at 10 µs, the native 31-section and 256-segment polyline cases take 41.04 s and 41.45 s online, respectively."
        }
      ],
      "X": 75,
      "Y": 420
    },
    {
      "Id": "step-translations",
      "Caption": "Production STEP translations",
      "Title": "Direct B-rep search completes six of eight production translation paths and agrees with the numerical reference on those six",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/generic-assembly-results.tex — tab:production-contact\nOne reference path is unresolved. OCCT advancement shares the reference distance kernel."
        }
      ],
      "X": 75,
      "Y": 540
    },
    {
      "Id": "refined-reducer",
      "Caption": "Refined RecurDyn comparison",
      "Title": "STEP with pair stiffness gives 0.210 rad/s middle-speed RMS difference and 17.55 N·m output-torque RMS difference over 0–1.26 s",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/sampled-dynamics-results.tex — tab:refined-reducer\nTorque is averaged over common 125 µs output intervals."
        }
      ],
      "X": 75,
      "Y": 660
    },
    {
      "Id": "discrete-scope",
      "Caption": "Discrete residual scope",
      "Title": "The enclosure controls the discrete equations for supported force callbacks. Step size still affects transition timing",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/Residual-Aware-CAD-Contact.tex — Discussion\ndocs/AES/method.tex — sec:method, eq:resid-error\ndocs/AES/published-validation.tex — tab:oscillator"
        }
      ],
      "X": 755,
      "Y": 180
    },
    {
      "Id": "reuse-cost",
      "Caption": "Reuse cost varies",
      "Title": "The cached bounded cam is faster than the tight bounded mode and slower than direct evaluation. The tested cached gear runs take longer than their tight bounded counterparts",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — sec:ablation\nThe reducer ablation covers a 0.2 s diagnostic through the first load transient."
        }
      ],
      "X": 755,
      "Y": 300
    },
    {
      "Id": "matched-scope",
      "Caption": "Comparison scope",
      "Title": "The specialized gear comparison holds the sampled projected contact law fixed. Time step and geometry resolution both affect the force error",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/force-kernel-results.tex — sec:industrial, Single-stage spur pair, Two-stage reducer"
        }
      ],
      "X": 755,
      "Y": 420
    },
    {
      "Id": "rotating-cam-budget",
      "Caption": "Rotating-cam task cap",
      "Title": "Under the 20,000-task cap, direct B-rep search meets the requested width on zero of 22 onset paths and returns wider contact brackets on three",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/generic-contact-results.tex — tab:cam-onset and the paragraph below it\nThe analytic cylinder–plane gap independently scores the brackets. The numerical and mesh setups have their own geometry and accuracy limits."
        }
      ],
      "X": 755,
      "Y": 540
    },
    {
      "Id": "shaft-agreement-scope",
      "Caption": "Shaft versus mesh response",
      "Title": "The comparison supports shaft-level load transfer. Mesh-frequency amplitudes remain sensitive to the stiffness model",
      "AdditionalNotes": [
        {
          "Title": "Manuscript sources",
          "Body": "docs/AES/sampled-dynamics-results.tex — paragraph after tab:refined-reducer"
        }
      ],
      "X": 755,
      "Y": 660
    }
  ],
